  "question": {
    "text": "The mean of a set of 30 observations is 75 . If each other observation is multiplied by a nonzero number $\\lambda$ and then each of them is decreased by 25 , their mean remains the same. The $\\lambda$ is equal to\nequal to $\\{0\\}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "61X1G",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{10}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ocOZn",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "99G1K",
      "text": "\n $\\frac{1}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3uxiV",
      "text": "\n $\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As mean is a linear operation, so if each observation is multiplied by $\\lambda$ and decreased by 25 then the mean becomes 75 $\\lambda-25$.\nAccording to the question,\n$$\n75 \\lambda-25=75 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
